  "details": "<p>The porticus itself is no longer extant. Its location can be pinpointed with accuracy, lying between the remains of the Theater of Pompey and the Area Sacra of Largo Argentina. The porticus is represented on several fragments of the Severan marble plan of the city of Rome.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A porticus built in 55 B.C. in connection with the Theater of Pompey. The Curia Pompei, site of Iulius Caesar's assassination in 44 B.C., was likely located within the portico.",
